# 35. REQUIRED ACCEPTANCE SCENARIOS

Verify the following end-to-end experiences.

SCENARIO 1: FIRST LEARNING SESSION
- Student selects Bangla or English.
- Creates an account.
- Selects academic class and subjects.
- Opens a subject.
- Completes a lesson.
- Starts Quick Practice.
- Answers a question.
- Receives correct feedback.
- Sees persisted progress.

SCENARIO 2: QUEST REWARD
- Student completes an eligible task.
- Backend validates completion.
- Quest progresses.
- Eligible reward is granted once.
- XP history updates.
- Dashboard reflects the actual result.

SCENARIO 3: FRIENDSHIP
- Student A searches Student B by StudyQuest ID.
- Sends a request.
- Student B receives the request.
- Student B accepts.
- Both see the friendship.

SCENARIO 4: PRIVATE MESSAGING
- Accepted friends open a conversation.
- Student A sends a message.
- The backend persists it.
- Student B receives it.
- Delivery state is accurate.
- Blocking prevents further contact.

SCENARIO 5: STUDY GROUP
- Student creates a private study group.
- Invites friends.
- Friends accept.
- Group membership is verified.
- Members exchange messages.
- Unauthorized users cannot access the group.

SCENARIO 6: MULTIPLAYER BATTLE
- Two actual students request compatible matches.
- Matchmaking pairs them.
- Both enter the same lobby.
- Countdown is synchronized.
- Questions are shared appropriately.
- Both submit answers.
- Backend evaluates answers.
- Final score is verified.
- Results are saved.

SCENARIO 7: LEADERBOARD
- Completed eligible matches affect appropriate ranking.
- Duplicate matches do not award repeated points.
- Personal position is correct.
- Weekly and seasonal results are separated.
- Historical rankings remain accessible.

SCENARIO 8: MOCK EXAM
- Student selects a real exam configuration.
- Starts the timed examination.
- Answers are saved.
- Student submits.
- Results are calculated.
- Answer review shows the correct approved explanation.

SCENARIO 9: PRIVACY
- Student A cannot read Student B's private conversations.
- A blocked account cannot bypass the restriction.
- A nonmember cannot open a private group.
- A student cannot alter their own verified score.

SCENARIO 10: LANGUAGE
- Student switches between Bangla and English.
- Navigation and interface update.
- Academic records remain intact.
- Text remains correctly displayed.

SCENARIO 11: OFFLINE
- Previously downloaded content remains available.
- Eligible practice progress is stored locally.
- The interface identifies unsynchronized records.
- Reconnection synchronizes without duplication.

SCENARIO 12: ACCOUNT DELETION
- Student initiates deletion.
- Confirmation occurs.
- Sessions are revoked.
- Applicable personal data is deleted or anonymized.
- Required retention is handled transparently.

